    {
      "id": "293",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 293,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "か何か and かどうか look similar but are used differently. か何か follows a noun and means 'or something,' as in お茶か何か飲みますか？ ('Would you like some tea or something?'). かどうか means 'whether or not' and expresses uncertainty, like 面白いかどうか分からない ('I don't know whether or not it's interesting.').",
        "first_relatable": {
